Fair use is not a print use standard.  There is no one answer on it,
because there is no "letter of the law" in fair use, though there are
extreme cases each way which are well defined.

Because there is no letter of the law, it's up to the court.  The court
will examine your *motives*, not the letter of what you wrote.  So
obviously contrived schemes to put silly commentary on Playboy photos
will never get bought as fair use.

Think about it.  If you were on the jury and asked to decide if the
person was exploiting the photo or really trying honestly to comment
on it, needing the photo as illustration, how would you judge?  That's
a good start in deciding if you have done fair use.
