Posting or emailing stolen documents IS a piracy issue, just like posting 
or emailing stolen scans of pretty women in the nude is.  Information piracy
is defined as the theft <and distribution> of stolen material covered by
copyright or trade secret.  Stealing "codez" (or passwords) and posting or 
emailing them certainly qualifies, as does sending giffy files around that
you do not own the rights to.

If you use the phone lines to do the deed you can be indicted for 
wire fraud.  If the transmission crosses state lines it can be a <federal>
issue at the government's whim.

